Subject: [PATCH] Input: zforce_ts - accept the "neonode_v2" touch state encoding

The zForce in the Netronix E60QH2 (firmware 0001.0000.0000.0001) reports
touch states 4/5/6 (down/move/up) and numbers contacts from 0, while the
driver expects 0/1/2 and contacts from 1. The UP state was never seen, so
BTN_TOUCH and the MT slot stayed pressed forever (and contact 0 selected
slot -1). Map the offset encoding to the standard one.

Raw point byte 4 captured on the device: 0x04 down, 0x05 move, 0x06 up.

--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/zforce_ts.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/zforce_ts.c
@@ -75,6 +75,11 @@
 #define STATE_DOWN			0
 #define STATE_MOVE			1
 #define STATE_UP			2
+/*
+ * Some firmware (e.g. Netronix E60QH2, "neonode_v2") reports the states
+ * offset by 4 and numbers the contacts from 0 instead of 1.
+ */
+#define STATE_V2_OFFSET			4
 
 #define SETCONFIG_DUALTOUCH		(1 << 0)
 
@@ -332,6 +337,10 @@
 
 		point.state = p[4] & 0x0f;
 		point.id = (p[4] & 0xf0) >> 4;
+		if (point.state >= STATE_V2_OFFSET) {
+			point.state -= STATE_V2_OFFSET;
+			point.id++;
+		}
 
 		/* determine touch major, minor and orientation */
 		point.area_major = max(p[5], p[6]);
